.TH SKEET 1 "2026" "skeet 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skeet \- terminal AI coding agent powered by local LLMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skeet
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skeet
is an interactive terminal AI coding agent in the style of Claude Code / OpenAI Codex,
running entirely on local hardware via Ollama or llama.cpp backends.
.PP
It provides a conversational REPL where an LLM can read files, search code, apply
patches, and run shell commands — all inside your project workspace — without sending
data to remote services.
.PP
The agent uses a structured tool loop: the model calls built-in tools (read_file, grep,
glob, edit_file, write_file, bash) and third-party plugins (native C ABI, Rust cdylib,
Lua scripts), accumulates tool results, and produces a final answer.  Context is managed
automatically and can be compacted at any time with \fB/compact\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Path to a TOML config file.  Defaults to
.I ~/.config/skeet/config.toml
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fIname\fR"
Model name to use (e.g.
.IR qwen2.5\-coder:7b ,
.IR codellama:13b ).
Overrides the value in the config file.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend " \fIname\fR"
Backend to use.  One of:
.RS
.IP "\fBollama\fR (default)"
Talks to a running Ollama daemon via its HTTP API.
.IP "\fBllama\fR"
Calls llama.cpp's \fBllama\-server\fR compatible REST endpoint directly.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " \fIurl\fR"
Backend base URL.  Defaults to
.I http://localhost:11434
for Ollama and
.I http://localhost:8080
for llama.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace " \fIdir\fR"
Root directory that the agent is allowed to read and modify.
Defaults to the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plugin " \fIpath\fR"
Load a dynamic library plugin (\fI.so\fR on Linux/macOS, \fI.dll\fR on Windows).
May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-lua " \fIpath\fR"
Load a Lua plugin script.  Requires LuaJIT at runtime (looked up via
.BR dlopen (3) ).
May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging (HTTP traffic, token counts, tool timings).
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH SLASH COMMANDS
Inside the interactive REPL the following commands are available:
.TP
.B /help
List all commands and tools.
.TP
.B /tools
Show registered tools with descriptions.
.TP
.B /model \fIname\fR
Switch to a different model mid-session.
.TP
.B /backend \fIname\fR
Switch backend (ollama | llama).
.TP
.B /compact
Summarise and discard old messages to free context window.
.TP
.B /session save \fIname\fR
Save current session to disk.
.TP
.B /session load \fIname\fR
Restore a saved session.
.TP
.B /session list
List saved sessions.
.TP
.B /tune
Run the hardware detector and print recommended GGUF parameters.
.TP
.B /clear
Clear screen.
.TP
.B /exit " | " /quit
Exit the agent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKEET_MODEL
Default model name (overridden by \fB\-m\fR).
.TP
.B SKEET_BACKEND
Default backend (overridden by \fB\-b\fR).
.TP
.B SKEET_HOST
Backend URL (overridden by \fB\-H\fR).
.TP
.B SKEET_WORKSPACE
Default workspace directory (overridden by \fB\-w\fR).
.TP
.B SKEET_LOG_LEVEL
Logging verbosity: \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.B SKEET_PERMISSIONS
Comma-separated list of allowed operations.
Possible values: \fBread\fR, \fBwrite\fR, \fBbash\fR, \fBnet\fR.
Defaults to \fBread,write,bash\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/skeet/config.toml
User configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/skeet/sessions/
Saved session files (JSON).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/skeet/history
REPL input history.
.TP
.I {workspace}/SKEET.md
Project-level conventions file.  If present, its contents are injected into
the model's system prompt at session start.
.TP
.I {workspace}/.skeet/plugins/*.lua
Project-local Lua plugins, auto-loaded at startup.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start an interactive session in the current directory with the default model:
.PP
.RS
.nf
skeet
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a specific model and backend:
.PP
.RS
.nf
skeet -m codellama:13b -b ollama
.fi
.RE
.PP
Point the agent at a different project:
.PP
.RS
.nf
skeet -w ~/projects/myapp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Load a Rust plugin and a Lua plugin:
.PP
.RS
.nf
skeet -p ./plugins/libskeet_rust_codex_tools.so -L ./plugins/example_plugin.lua
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with verbose logging to debug HTTP calls:
.PP
.RS
.nf
skeet -v
.fi
.RE
